                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.512/1025: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-06-05T13:00:00-04:00">June 5, 1930—1
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>182. Your 374, May 27, 6 p.m. You are authorized in your discretion and on
                    specific request of American interest concerned to protest to <hi
                        rendition="#italic">de facto</hi> Northern authorities if and when such
                    authorities impose taxes on American petroleum or other products when
                    accompanied by transit passes issued by the recognized and appropriate Chinese
                    authorities purporting to exempt the products in question from all taxation in
                    transit.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
